      "writtenOn": "2022-04-26T20:37:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about re-enabling on physical charger disconnection?  There could be hypothetical problems with CC line stability that would charge cycle with \"disconnect\" detected periodically, but you\u0027d be covered for more common scenarios like hard reset cycling on the PD connection. \n\nThe alternative would be letting the OS clear it via host command once we\u0027ve had a sufficiently stable boot or similar. Waiting until EC reset just seems somewhat confusing for customers who plug in a bad charger once.\n\nOr I suppose you could keep a count within a certain time window.  So many options",
      "revId": "b92d646ddd03bc146961b2d1e0cc51960e502d0b",
